[statement]
A choice made for a name packages only provide does not steer a name some
package carries that the request names away from its choice: `x`,
requested and decided first, takes `x` 3, its best candidate. `y1`, the
best candidate for `Y`, needs `w`, which only `x` 1 provides; apk keeps
`x` 3 and takes `y2` for `Y`. Contrast
`a-requested-name-some-package-carries-follows-a-carried-name` and
`a-requested-name-some-package-carries-is-steered-from-a-package-it-does-not-admit`.

[repository]
P:x
V:3

P:x
V:1
p:w=2

P:y1
V:1
k:5
p:Y
D:w

P:y2
V:1
k:1
p:Y

[request]
x
Y

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install x 3
install y2 1
